contracts:
  stdout data-only; stderr diagnostics/progress.
  No implicit TUI when automation flags set or stdout non-TTY.
  Color auto off when non-TTY unless forced.
  Use --quiet to silence info logs in robot runs.
  JSON errors only to stderr.
  Swarm status/work-packet/lint are read-only advisory surfaces: they do not claim beads, send mail, reserve files, force-release, run builds, mutate git, or delete data.
  Swarm stale detection is advisory; takeover-like actions require explicit coordination and human/agent confirmation outside cass.
  Swarm evidence defaults are privacy-safe: raw session content and full mail bodies are omitted unless a future explicit redacted evidence opt-in allows snippets.
  Rerank is off by default. --rerank uses qwen3-local with N=200/K=5. --rrf-limit N and --rerank-limit K are independent; all actual N candidates are scored before the K-result page is displayed.
  Choose --rerank-provider qwen3-local|bge-local|openrouter-qwen3-8b|openrouter-cohere-4-fast|openrouter-voyage-2.5-lite. --provider still filters the session source.
  score keeps its search meaning. rerank_score is separate and null when unscored; minimal/summary omit it unless explicitly added. JSON/compact/JSONL/TOON carry _meta.rerank without --robot-meta.
  Failure keeps original order and K-result paging; failure_reason is a short code, not response text. No automatic backend switch. Actual identity and unproven counts stay null.
  First page: cass search "auth error" --mode lexical --agent codex --rerank --rerank-provider bge-local --rrf-limit 200 --rerank-limit 5 --json
  Next page: cass search "auth error" --mode lexical --agent codex --rerank --rerank-provider bge-local --rrf-limit 200 --rerank-limit 5 --json --cursor "<next_cursor>"
  Repeat the original query, N/K, provider and filters. Only display fields and content/token budgets may change. Pages reuse a fixed window; current model requests and duration are zero, first-call facts remain. A reduced page advances by its delivered count.
